.TH env_pick 3
.SH NAME
env_pick \- return the first environment variable
.SH SYNTAX
.B #include <env.h>

.B char* env_pick(void);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B env_pick
returns a pointer to the first entry in the current process environment array (\fIenviron\fP).
.SH RETURN VALUE
A pointer to the first string in \fIenviron\fP, or NULL if empty.